  "body": "Source: the second review of PR #2488. Comment: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2488#issuecomment-6978941310\n\nNone of these items is a defect in posted output.\n\n## Items\n\n1. Split two long files. Each file is over the 400-line limit.\n   - `crates/app/tests/tool_numbers.rs` has 476 lines. Split it along a domain seam.\n   - `crates/app/src/commands/tool_import.rs` has 402 lines. Split it along a domain seam.\n   - The `#[test]` count must not go down.\n\n2. Add two legacy-load tests. The current legacy-load test uses two tools. Their add order equals their name order. So it does not prove the load order.\n   - Add a test for an old project whose tool order is not the name order.\n   - Add a test for an old project that mixes numbered and unnumbered tools.\n\n3. Remove the `u32::MAX` fallback. `crates/app/src/tool_numbers.rs:467` uses `u32::MAX` when no number is free for an unnumbered tool. Only test fixtures reach this line. Replace the fallback with a refusal that names the tool.\n\n4. Remove a dead branch. `crates/ui/src/state.rs:3450` has the `None => \"number cleared\"` message. `SetToolNumber` refuses `None` now, so this branch cannot run. Remove it.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Both split files are under about 400 lines.\n- The two new tests pass.\n- No `.nc` or `.cl` golden file changes.\n",
